invariant: INV-10
file: quic_packet.c
catches: quic_test
reason: the one added to pn_mask in 32 bits wraps to zero at a 4-byte
  packet number, whose window is 2^32, so quic_pn_decode adds and takes
  away no window at that length and recovers the wrong number once the
  truncated one passes a window's edge. The nonce is built from that
  number, so the peer's packet does not open. test_pn_decode requires both
  window edges at every encoded length, 1 to QUIC_PN_MAX_LEN bytes.

--- old
    uint64_t pn_win = pn_mask + 1;
--- new
    uint64_t pn_win = (uint64_t)(uint32_t)(pn_mask + 1);
